From 39806118446ca8f752c275fa36487b38c642a2c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HuJK <gh@hujk.org>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:18:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] k27: the console selector stays writable on macOS
 (Droid-VM/UniXNU-droidvm 06c78e6 droidvm-macos-console-switch.patch)

With the serial console (serial=3), the display driver hands the console to serial as WindowServer takes the display
(PE_initialize_console kPEDisableScreen -> switch_to_serial_console), which writes cons_ops_index; arm64 keeps it
SECURITY_READ_ONLY_LATE, and the write after lockdown panicked the guest right after its first frame. x86 keeps it
writable for the same reason.
---
 osfmk/console/serial_console.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
index 11d9eb4..3a8ca40 100644
--- a/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
+++ b/osfmk/console/serial_console.c
@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ SECURITY_READ_ONLY_EARLY(struct console_ops) cons_ops[] = {
 
 SECURITY_READ_ONLY_EARLY(uint32_t) nconsops = (sizeof cons_ops / sizeof cons_ops[0]);
 
-#if __x86_64__
+#if __x86_64__ || XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX
 uint32_t cons_ops_index = VC_CONS_OPS;
 #else
 SECURITY_READ_ONLY_LATE(uint32_t) cons_ops_index = VC_CONS_OPS;
